---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Legal Notice & Privacy" description="Legal notice and privacy information.">
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container article">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Legal Notice &amp; Privacy</h1>

      <div class="card notice">
        <strong>Placeholder — fill in before publishing.</strong>
        <p>
          Under German law (§ 5 TMG), commercially operated and generally also
          permanently run private websites are required to carry a legal notice
          ("Impressum") with a postal address that can accept service of process. Add
          the name, address, and contact details (email/phone) of the responsible
          parties before the site goes live. When in doubt, a brief legal review is
          worthwhile – this is not legal advice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Information pursuant to § 5 TMG</h2>
      <p>
        [Name, address]<br />
        [Contact: email, phone if applicable]
      </p>

      <h2>Responsible for content</h2>
      <p>[Name(s) of the operators]</p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is built as a static website with no backend of its own. If forms,
        analytics tools, or comment functionality are added later, this privacy notice
        must be extended accordingly (legal basis, retention period, recipients, right
        of withdrawal).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article { max-width: 720px; }
  .notice {
    background: rgba(154, 74, 43, 0.08);
    border-color: var(--color-warn);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
</style>
